-- the head of a path given to what makes a text from it; a path holding no one module (it holds
-- alternatives, or nothing) is not written from. A machine built before the head could be read
-- (2026-11-22) answers nothing, and the writer is told to build it
hy-tip-then : List Word → List Word → List (List Word) → (List Word → List (List Word) → Proc W Unit) → Proc W Unit
hy-tip-then path ids nil k = h-fail (list-append path " holds no one module now (alternatives, or nothing), or the machine is older than this tool (run make): nothing written")
hy-tip-then path ids (cons p ps) k = k ids (cons p ps)
